    "chunk_text": "Forensic Science: The silent guardian of justice in Sri Lanka\n\nWhen a serious crime occurs, the public often sees police officers, detectives, and court proceedings. However, behind every successful criminal investigation lies another group of professionals who rarely appear in the spotlight\u2014forensic scientists. Working quietly in laboratories, they use science to uncover the truth and provide evidence that helps ensure justice is served.\n\nForensic science is the application of scientific knowledge to legal investigations. It involves examining physical evidence collected from crime scenes, victims, suspects, and other relevant sources. Unlike eyewitness testimony, which can sometimes be inaccurate or influenced by memory, forensic evidence is objective and based on scientific principles. It, therefore, plays a crucial role in both convicting the guilty and protecting innocent individuals from wrongful accusations.\n\nSri Lanka has a proud history of applying science to the administration of justice. The Government Analyst\u2019s Department has served the nation for more than a century as the country\u2019s principal forensic science institution. Today, its highly trained forensic scientists provide scientific services to the Sri Lanka Police, the Criminal Investigation Department (CID), the judiciary, and other law enforcement agencies. Through the use of modern technology and internationally accepted scientific methods, they assist in solving thousands of criminal and civil cases each year."
