    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "5ae400d9fcc67e771be0a0dc7826ad70",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1487,
    "chunk_text": "Daraz Sri Lanka joins Dialog Pay merchant ecosystem\n\nFrom left: Muditha Premarathne - Vice President, Digital Platforms and Partnerships, Dialog Axiata PLC; Lasantha Theverapperuma - Group Chief Marketing Officer, Dialog Axiata PLC and Rukshan Xavier - Managing Director, Daraz Sri Lanka\n\nDialog Axiata PLC announced that customers can now make secure digital payments using Dialog Pay when receiving Cash on Delivery (COD) orders from Daraz.\n\nAs Sri Lanka\u2019s leading online marketplace, Daraz joins the Dialog Pay merchant ecosystem, extending the convenience of digital payments to customers\u2019 doorsteps. Customers who select COD at checkout can simply scan the Dialog Pay QR code presented by the Daraz rider upon delivery and enjoy complimentary Dialog data rewards on every eligible transaction.\n\nCommenting on the partnership, Rukshan Xavier, Managing Director, Daraz Sri Lanka said, \u201cAt Daraz, we believe digital payments will play an increasingly important role in shaping the future of e-commerce in Sri Lanka. Our partnership with Dialog reflects our shared commitment to making online shopping more seamless, secure and accessible while supporting the country\u2019s transition towards a more digitally connected and cash-light economy.\n\nBy combining Dialog\u2019s digital payment capabilities with Daraz\u2019s e-commerce reach, we aim to give customers greater convenience, choice and value at checkout, while encouraging wider adoption of digital payments across the country.\u201d"
  },
