    "chunk_size_bytes": 1477,
    "chunk_text": "Week ends in red\n\nThe ASPI closed in red as a result of price losses in counters such as LOLC Holdings, John Keells Holdings and Cargills with the turnover crossing Rs. 722 Mn.\n\nMeanwhile, the S&P SL20 edged down. High net worth and institutional investor participation was noted in Chevron Lubricants, Lanka IOC and ACL Cables. Mixed interest was observed in Sampath Bank, John Keells\n\nHoldings and Lanka Milk Foods whilst retail interest was noted in UB Finance Company, Renuka Agri Foods and ACME Printing & Packaging. Furthermore, foreigners closed as net sellers.\n\nDuring the week, the ASPI and the S&P SL20 lost 1.7% and 1.3% respectively, whilst recording an average daily turnover of Rs. 1.11 Bn.\n\nThe Banking sector was the top contributor to the market turnover (due to Sampath Bank) whilst the sector index gained 0.18%. The share price of Sampath Bank closed flat at Rs 137.00.\n\nCapital Goods sector was the second highest contributor to the market turnover (due to John Keells Holdings) whilst the sector index decreased by 0.12%. The share price of John Keells Holdings moved down by Rs 0.10 (0.50%) to close at Rs 19.90.\n\nLanka IOC, Chevron Lubricants and Lanka Milk Foods were also included amongst the top turnover contributors. The share price of Lanka IOC gained Rs 0.25 (0.18%) to close at Rs 136.50. The share price of Chevron Lubricants recorded a loss of Rs 0.25 (0.13%) to close at Rs 197.75. The share price of Lanka Milk Foods closed flat at Rs 84.50."
