    "md5": "bafd452f84e6becf19b55d5b36cdf95f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1983,
    "chunk_text": "FACETS Sri Lanka 2027: 34th edition of a dazzling legacy\n\nFrom left: EDB Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe, SLGJA Vice President Operations and COO Shezan Mansoor, SLGJA President Akram Cassim, FACETS Sri Lanka 2027 Chairman Shezmin Mansoor, National Gem and Jewellery Authority Chairman Prof. S.P. Chaminda and Cinnamon Life - City of Dreams Hotel Manager Roshan George\n\nFACETS 2027 Chairman Shezmin Mansoor announces dates for next three years\n\nThe 34th edition of FACETS Sri Lanka, organised by the Sri Lanka Gem and Jewellery Association (SLGJA), will take place from January 4 to 6, 2027, at the iconic Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams Colombo.\n\nThe landmark event will bring together over one hundred exhibitors representing the finest gem and jewellery companies in the country. Buyers from the USA, Europe, the Middle East, India, China, Thailand and other key markets will converge in Colombo to experience Sri Lanka\u2019s unmatched craftsmanship and gemstone excellence.\n\nA press conference to announce the 34th edition brought together key stakeholders from across the public and private sectors, with several distinguished guests sharing their views on the significance of the exhibition and the continued growth of Sri Lanka\u2019s gem and jewellery industry. Among them were National Gem and Jewellery Authority Chairman (NGJA) Prof. S.P. Chaminda, Export Development Board (EDB) Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe and Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams Hotel Manager Roshan George, who reaffirmed their respective organisations\u2019 commitment to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s premier international gem and jewellery exhibition.\n\nThe 34th edition of FACETS Sri Lanka will include dedicated sections that showcase the island\u2019s world\u2011renowned sapphires and contemporary luxury jewellery, while a series of special events \u2014 including Sapphire Night, Story Corner, Power Breakfast, Mine Tour and Port City Tour \u2014 will create opportunities for networking, knowledge\u2011sharing and collaboration."
