    "chunk_text": "Egg prices to increase from tomorrow\n\nColombo, July 19 (Daily Mirror) - The All Ceylon Egg Producers\u2019 Association said that egg prices will increase from tomorrow (20), citing rising production challenges and feed shortages.\n\nAccording to the association, the price of a white egg will increase to Rs. 41, while a red egg will be sold at Rs. 42.\n\nAssociation President Sarath Ratnayake said the price revision was necessitated by difficulties affecting poultry feed supplies, including a shortage of maize and a decline in overall egg production.\n\nHe further stated that egg production has dropped by 20\u201330% due to ongoing challenges faced by the poultry industry, leading to reduced supply in the market."
