    "chunk_text": "AA3 Holdings unveils Lanka\u2019s largest ex-stock heavy equipment showroom in Kiribathgoda\n\nAA3 Holdings has opened Sri Lanka\u2019s largest ex-stock heavy equipment showroom and fully equipped workshop in Kiribathgoda, responding to rising industry demand. The state-of-the-art facility houses the country\u2019s biggest inventory of ready-to-deliver machinery, enabling faster customer access and strengthening the company\u2019s market position.\n\nChairman Supun Perera called the expansion a strategic milestone to enhance service capabilities and deliver an unparalleled ownership experience. AA3 Holdings, a subsidiary of the Udeshi Group with roots dating to 1986, is a leading provider of construction and mining equipment in Sri Lanka and the Maldives.\n\nThe new showroom lets clients explore top-tier earthmoving, excavation, and road construction machinery firsthand. Its advanced workshop features cutting-edge diagnostic tools and specialized repair equipment for rapid, precision servicing. After-sales support includes factory-trained technicians focused on maximizing uptime and operational efficiency.\n\nCASE Vice President Emre Karazli noted Sri Lanka\u2019s growing infrastructure and road network opportunities, emphasizing the brand\u2019s commitment to environmentally responsible, high-performance equipment. He also mentioned CASE\u2019s ongoing factory development in India.\n\nShalahh Chaathurvedi, CASE Managing Director, announced that Colombo will host the company\u2019s annual dealer convention over two days, with over 150 international delegates \u2013 positioning it as one of Sri Lanka\u2019s largest MICE events this year.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
