    "md5": "f9205b2300b47c27aa7693d3b07fdab6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1281,
    "chunk_text": "Conversely, Vietnam has also become an increasingly attractive destination for Sri Lankan outbound travelers. In 2025, Vietnam welcomed a historic 22 million international global visitors, which included over 14,000 Sri Lankan travelers. The Ambassador pointed out Vietnam\u2019s reciprocal appeal, highlighting the country\u2019s natural landscapes, vibrant cities, rich cultural heritage, renowned cuisine, and most importantly, its hospitality and friendliness.\n\nThe economic ripple effects of uncovering this hidden gem will extend far beyond the hospitality sector. Stronger air connectivity will generate stronger economic connectivity, the Ambassador stressed, emphasizing that an influx of visitors will create greater demand for hotels, transportation, retail, trade, and investment opportunities.\n\nEnsuring the long-term commercial success of the Ho Chi Minh City-Colombo route will require a coordinated effort from government agencies, tourism authorities, and local travel enterprises. \u201cTourism cooperation should always be a two-way street bringing mutual benefit to both countries,\u201d the Ambassador concluded, encouraging Vietnamese and Sri Lankan tourism enterprises to work closely to design attractive tour packages and maximize this unprecedented connectivity. (NF)"
  },
