    "md5": "72a4c2ec7012edf60414a344ebc4b65b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1918,
    "chunk_text": "Sir Susantha toured his constituency, then stretching into what is now Bandaragama and Kesbewa, on horseback, his chauffeur-driven limousine trailing empty behind him. The clatter of hooves on the road would wake the neighbourhood children, myself among them, then just four years old, and we would run to the garden to watch him pass.\n\nLesley Goonewardene, son of a prominent Panadura physician and himself a wealthy LSSP leader, had lost the seat to Susantha de Fonseka in 1936 and moved on to contest Colombo North instead. That left the Panadura LSSP with only one candidate willing to take on the de Fonseka name: Henry Peiris, the party\u2019s bicycle-riding bulletin editor, standing under Dr. Colvin R. de Silva\u2019s breakaway Bolshevik-Leninist Party. Against all the weight of Panadura\u2019s landed gentry, he won.\n\nI came to know the third of these men in the early 1970s. He lived down shanty infested Muhandiram Lane in Kollupitiya, among the labouring families of the wattas, in one of Colombo\u2019s poorer settlements. He had once served as City Father for the Kollupitiya ward, a ward that, oddly, also took in the affluent Cinnamon Gardens. D.S. Mallawaarachchi, known to the poor as \u201cMal Sahodaraya,\u201d ran a small union office for private-sector minor employees affiliated with the LSSP. I encountered his work directly while employed at Shaw Wallace & Hedges, the European-managed firm whose labourers largely belonged to his union.\n\nOne day, a storeroom labourer named Bandaiya, distrustful of his own union, sought Mallawaarachchi\u2019s help in drafting a letter about a workplace dispute. Mallawaarachchi typed the letter twice and spent nearly two hours ensuring it was properly prepared. When Bandaiya tried to press a five-rupee note\u2014the equivalent of a full day\u2019s wage\u2014into his hand, Mallawaarachchi flung it away and snapped, \u201cGive me the letter. If you have money, go and hire a lawyer.\u201d"
  },
