    "md5": "dba16940f5e440199c000bc9f65ccb1e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1852,
    "chunk_text": "BNI Sri Lanka National Conference on 24 July to bring together visionary biz leaders\n\nBusiness Network International (BNI) Sri Lanka, the local chapter of the world\u2019s largest business networking and referral organisation, will host the BNI Sri Lanka National Conference 2026 on 24 July at Cinnamon Lakeside Colombo, bringing together BNI members from across Sri Lanka and the global BNI network for a day of inspiration, learning, and meaningful business connections.\n\nHeld annually as BNI Sri Lanka\u2019s flagship event, the National Conference celebrates entrepreneurship, leadership, and collaboration while reinforcing the organisation\u2019s commitment to helping businesses grow through trusted relationships and the philosophy of Givers Gain. As part of one of the world\u2019s largest business referral networks, the conference provides members with a unique opportunity to exchange ideas, strengthen professional relationships, and gain valuable insights from internationally respected business leaders.\n\nThis year\u2019s conference will feature two distinguished keynote speakers whose leadership journeys have shaped globally recognised organisations.\n\nSri Lankan entrepreneur ODEL and Embark Founder Otara Gunewardene will share her journey of building one of the country\u2019s most iconic retail brands while demonstrating how innovation, purpose-driven leadership, and sustainability can create enduring business success.\n\nJoining her as the international keynote speaker is India\u2019s Zoho Corporation Director and Zoho Schools of Learning President Rajendran Dandapani. Representing one of the world\u2019s leading technology companies, Dandapani will share global perspectives on entrepreneurship, leadership, innovation, and talent development, drawing on Zoho\u2019s internationally recognised people-first approach to building sustainable businesses."
