    "chunk_text": "Former IGP C.D. Wickramaratne\u2019s final rites to be held with full police honours\n\n- Wickremaratne\u2019s death a great loss to the country: Maithripala Sirisena\n\nColombo, July 20 (Daily Mirror) - The final rites of former Inspector General of Police (IGP) C.D. Wickramaratne will be held with full police honours at the Borella Cemetery this afternoon, Police Spokesman ASP F.U Wootler said.\n\n\u200bThe 35th Inspector General of Police (IGP) of Sri Lanka, C.D. Wickramaratne, died at his residence in Malabe on Friday from a gunshot wound. Police currently suspect his death to be a suicide, as initial investigations revealed that he had reportedly shot himself using his security officer's firearm.\n\nMeanwhile, police have launched a specialist forensic examination to determine how the former IGP sustained the gunshot wound.\n\nHis mortal remains have been sent to the Government Analyst for further examination.\n\nPolice also said that the former IGP's mobile phone had been taken into police custody and would be examined following a court order as part of the ongoing investigation.\n\nThe pistol believed to have been used in the shooting has also been taken into police custody and will be sent to the Government Analyst for forensic analysis.\n\nStatements have been recorded from the former IGP's spouse and the three police officers assigned to his security.\n\nHis remains were placed at a private funeral parlour in Borella last morning, where members of the public, political figures, former state officials and senior police officers gathered to pay their final respects.\n\nFormer President Ranil Wickramesinghe and several other prominent figures were among those who visited the funeral parlour to pay tribute to the former police chief.\n\nMeanwhile, former President Maithripala Sirisena described Wickremaratne\u2019s death at the age of 63 as an even greater loss, saying a person at that age is at the peak of intelligence, maturity and ability to serve society."
